ceiver.settings_templates: check_feature reprogrammable-keys [REPROG CONTROLS V4] error 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'remappable_to'\r\n2025-01-01 14:21:33,300,300    ERROR [SolaarListener:hidraw2] logitech_receiver.settings_templates: check_feature divert-keys [REPROG CONTROLS V4] error 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flags'\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n\r\n**Describe the bug**\r\nWhen I connect my logitech lift, the settings are not restored fully in most of the cases. Sometimes only 4 restored:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/013c0588-26f7-44c7-954d-6c203ae7aafa)\r\nSometimes only 3:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a2c0224-2076-43b5-b765-ec284a7d9a35)\r\n\r\nThe number of restored settings is always random, so I need to disconnect-reconnect the mouse (I do it by clicking 'switch to the next device' button on the mouse) until all 5 settings are restored. Sometimes, when all five settings are restored, the battery charge is shown incorretly as 0:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0fb5860-ac01-4850-b763-4cf9af370c21)\r\n\r\n\r\nHere are some logs:\r\n[2.log.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18285708/2.log.txt)\r\n[4.log.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18285701/4.log.txt)\r\n[good.log.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18285709/good.log.txt)\r\n",
