        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:13:24Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:13:24Z",
        "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
        "body": "It seems that the problem stems from `gameinput.h` being found in configure, but the compiler fails to find it while building SDL for some reason. [Our last successful run](https://github.com/ppy/SDL3-CS/actions/runs/11456516812/job/31874820196) reported `Performing Test HAVE_GAMEINPUT_H - Failed`, so I guess something may have changed in GHA Windows image.\r\n\r\nWe can work around this issue by patching SDL to never include `gameinput.h`. Removing GameInput joystick support is not fatal as it is not used by default on Windows (non-Xbox), anyway.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/3197e27b59416442b2051b8d0dc1d4eb2a7732a0/include/SDL3/SDL_hints.h#L1314",
