        "body": "I went to do this, and realized that `tx_log` is actually being referenced when it creates a fee event. As far as I can tell though its only used to determine the sequence index. The only attribute here that isn't being used is `action_items`. So since most of `DecoderContext`'s attributes are actually referenced in `_decode_swap` I think keeping it like this is probably best. Also this way its simpler in the v5 decoder where there it directly passes the context.\r\n\r\nI've updated the comment here and also changed it to use the last log event instead of the first so it for sure uses a higher sequence index for fee events.",
